# --- Line endings ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Normalise text files to LF in the repository regardless of each machine's
# core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a teammate whose Git is configured differently
# commits whole-file diffs after changing one line, and nobody can review anything.
#
# This line MUST stay first. .gitattributes is last-match-wins, and `*` matches binary
# assets too — a `* text=auto` placed below the LFS entries would override their `-text`
# and start line-ending-converting .uasset files, which corrupts them.
* text=auto

# Parsed by cmd.exe, which has known quirks with LF-only labels and goto.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Must keep LF even when checked out on Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf

# --- Binary assets, tracked by Git LFS ----------------------------------------------
# `-text` disables line-ending conversion entirely. This matters more than it looks: an
# LFS pointer file is plain text, so `text=auto` above would otherwise normalise it.
#
# When UEGitPlugin is set up (see docs/PIPELINE.md §2 and §9), replace this block with
# the plugin's reference .gitattributes and add the `lockable` flag to .uasset/.umap.
*.uasset filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.umap filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.wav filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.fbx filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
